+# Sixteen prioritized investigation audits — planning snapshot
+
+October 26, 2026. This version supersedes the *ordering and acquisition status*
+of [v1](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/bb9e9c5d6fd30ec3bb3fbc5359f388ef8c8c0db2/investigation/broader-evidence/documentary-crosswalk-2026-10-26/NEXT-RECORDS-v1.md), which remains unchanged. These are planned audits,
+not new historical findings or permission for outreach, fees or publication.
+The [structured to-dos](audit-todos-v1.json) retain exact incoming wording,
+existing B/H/S IDs, source hashes/locators where already available, unresolved
+passage/version gaps, supporting and contrary material, dependencies, tests and
+observable completion criteria. Missing metadata remains explicitly pending.
+
+**Next substantive audit: CIA hold, claimed FBI notification and later oversight
+discovery.** Those are three linked questions to test, not a presumed single act.
+Our self-audit applies throughout and does not require completing every film
+attribution before obtaining the next CIA record.
+
+| Priority | Additive IDs | Task / discriminating comparison | State |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| 1 | AUD001, AUD002, AUD003 | PRIORITY NEXT: CIA information hold, claimed FBI notification, and late oversight disclosure. | Planned; existing summary review reused where specified; new target audits unrun at native intake; publication is separate |
+| 2 | AUD004 | FBI informant handling and payment. | Planned; existing summary review reused where specified; new target audits unrun at native intake; publication is separate |
+| 3 | AUD005, AUD006 | FAA/NORAD and Mineta chronology. | Planned; existing summary review reused where specified; new target audits unrun at native intake; publication is separate |
+| 4 | AUD007 | Interrogation-dependent planning claims. | Planned; existing summary review reused where specified; new target audits unrun at native intake; publication is separate |
+| 5 | AUD008 | Presidential warnings. | Planned; existing summary review reused where specified; new target audits unrun at native intake; publication is separate |
+| 6 | AUD009, AUD010, AUD011 | Evidence preservation and destruction. | Planned; existing summary review reused where specified; new target audits unrun at native intake; publication is separate |
+| 7 | AUD012, AUD013, AUD014, AUD015 | Next-tier financial allegations. | Planned; existing summary review reused where specified; new target audits unrun at native intake; publication is separate |
+| Throughout | AUD016 | Audit our own evaluation across every track. | Planned; existing summary review reused where specified; new target audits unrun at native intake; publication is separate |
+
+## Already recovered and still outstanding
+
+- The bank/telephone tranche at commit
+  `bb9e9c5d6fd30ec3bb3fbc5359f388ef8c8c0db2` is published. Its June23 AT&T
+  carrier sample, subpoena return and loading documentation were obtained.
+  Original bank exhibits Ex550/FBI8057, KSA Ex91/FBI2808–09, teller statement
+  and February4 cellular roots/Ex12A remain outstanding. Preserve the amount/
+  sign, date and22/27 count conflicts; table rows are not unique conversations.
+  Current detail: [published bank/telephone record](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/bb9e9c5d6fd30ec3bb3fbc5359f388ef8c8c0db2/investigation/broader-evidence/bank-phone-records-2026-10-26/RECORD.md)
+  and [published bank/telephone next records](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/bb9e9c5d6fd30ec3bb3fbc5359f388ef8c8c0db2/investigation/broader-evidence/bank-phone-records-2026-10-26/NEXT-RECORDS.md).
+- The full six-page April20,2004 Commission witness memorandum was recovered;
+  do not reacquire it as a missing record. Earlier full FBI interviews and
+  litigation exhibits/depositions remain targets. The separate
+  operational follow-up was local/unpublished at native intake. A selected
+  operational report and bank integration were subsequently published at
+  [commit838af603](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/commit/838af60393017b74e3fee08bd190bb7a9e8a0f04).
+  That later publication does not publish every underlying local source or
+  change the outstanding-original requirements. This backlog retains its
+  earlier intake flags as a dated snapshot; those flags are not live status.
+- Retain the v1 original-record targets not displaced by this priority change:
+  **BR01 bank/carrier roots**, **BR02 restaurant/witness originals**, and
+  **BR05 Saudi litigation drawing/video/expert/custody exhibits**. They remain
+  open alongside the new next CIA audit; no missing exhibit is silently dropped.
+  BR03 CIA and BR04 source handling are refined by AUD001–AUD004.
+- The current INS-authorization trace remains intact in its existing research
+  checkout. The new audit order neither replaces its findings nor implies its
+  unredacted approval/routing and result-dissemination gaps are resolved.
+- Published **M001–M134**, the original assessment, 247-row B/H crosswalk and
+  existing source findings/chain map remain unchanged. AUD IDs are task IDs,
+  not new M IDs or additional independent evidence.
+
+## Completion and provenance rules
+
+Track planned, acquired, inspected, verified and published separately. Acquiring
+a report is not acquiring the originals it describes; verifying source wording
+is not establishing historical purpose. Keep missing, demonstrably withheld,
+lost and destroyed records separate. Preserve negative results and alternative
+hypotheses, exact film cut/time or explicit unknown, and the evidence that would
+change each conclusion. Connected circumstantial evidence can matter without a
+confession; a demonstrated link and independent chains still require testing.
+
+For FAA chronology retain the distinct DOT notification and liaison/bridge
+findings. For preservation maintain separate FAA witness-cassette, CIA tape and
+WTC steel chains; do not merge purposes. For briefings test the claimed71-item
+release using individual dated products, recipients, delivery and actions.
+Interrogation dependence is claim-specific, without counting later repetition
+or post2004 evidence as independent inputs to the2004 report.
+
+[Task/priority/source coverage](COVERAGE.json) ·
+[publication provenance and adaptations](PROVENANCE.json) ·
+[public additions diff](TEXT-CHANGES.patch).
+
+## Publication and verification scope
+
+This publishes the frozen planning baseline. The per-task acquired/inspected/
+verified/published flags preserve their native intake meanings; this public
+planning artifact does not claim that the historical audits have been completed.
+Later local investigative results are outside this packet. Publishing the plan
+is separate from verifying its underlying allegations or obtaining every target.
+
+Run `python3 verify_backlog.py` from this folder to check task/priority/source
+coverage, packaged hashes and references. The verifier uses existing Git objects
+for reference targets omitted by a sparse checkout. It performs no network calls,
+source-authentication test or historical experiment. [Requested tracks](REQUEST.md)
+retain the exact eight audit-scope blocks. [Manifest](MANIFEST.json) pins the
+packaged files; its hash checks are preservation checks, not historical proof.

