+          "block": "P097",
+          "line": 97,
+          "text": "By mid-February, the CIR had not been sent to the FBI and was still in draft form in the CIA’s computer system. CIA records show that Dwight e-mailed a CIA contractor who handled computer matters and asked him to delete several draft cables in the computer system unrelated to this matter, but to save the draft CIR concerning Mihdhar. The contractor accessed the draft cable in the system the next day.",
+          "status": "Previously extracted source passage retained; this intake does not newly resolve historical truth",
