+          "exact_original_wording": "| **The CIA explicitly stopped dissemination of information about a future hijacker’s U.S. visa.** | The DOJ Inspector General documented a January 2000 instruction to hold a report intended for the FBI concerning Mihdhar. It was never sent. Another CIA cable said the information had already been passed to the FBI, but investigators could not corroborate that assertion. **This identifies a specific intervention and an unexplained contradiction.** The reason for the intervention remains unresolved. [oig.justice.gov](https://oig.justice.gov/sites/default/files/archive/special/0506/chapter5.htm?utm_source=chatgpt.com) |",
