+          "line_end": 8,
+          "exact_original_wording": "| **That same critical document was initially absent from the oversight investigation.** | The Inspector General discovered the draft only in February 2004, after noticing its title in another records list. It had not previously been supplied to either the DOJ review or the CIA Inspector General’s review. Its discovery required further interviews and delayed the investigation. **There were therefore two distinct failures: dissemination before the attack and completeness of disclosure afterward.** Their connection and intent were not established. [oig.justice.gov](https://oig.justice.gov/sites/default/files/archive/special/0506/chapter5.htm?utm_source=chatgpt.com) |",
