+        },
+        {
+          "block": "P026",
+          "line": 26,
+          "text": "In addition, a member of the CIA General Counsel’s staff conducted additional searches for documents relevant to particular disputed issues. As a result of that review, copies of additional relevant documents were also made available for our review.",
+          "status": "Previously extracted source passage retained; this intake does not newly resolve historical truth",
+          "source_url": "https://oig.justice.gov/sites/default/files/archive/special/0506/chapter5.htm",
+          "native_extraction_sha256": "10082d26b9ac6158b13f7ded9319548945debd19f4606451925537b9db6b865a",
+          "attachment_note": "Native extraction omitted; P-block/line identifiers are retained extraction locators, not official PDF pagination."
+        },
+        {
+          "block": "P027",
+          "line": 27,
+          "text": "In response to the JICI report issued in December 2002, the CIA OIG initiated a review in February 2003 of the CIA actions related to the September 11 attacks. In July 2003 the CIA OIG review team informed us it had several more documents that were relevant to our review. These documents were made available to us to review, and redacted copies of the documents were provided to us in November 2003. The CIA OIG review team also provided additional relevant documents and information to us that it found during the course of its review.",
+          "status": "Previously extracted source passage retained; this intake does not newly resolve historical truth",
+          "source_url": "https://oig.justice.gov/sites/default/files/archive/special/0506/chapter5.htm",
